---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Freighthub"
  description="What Freighthub processes when you read a page or send an email: server logs, correspondence, no accounts, no analytics cookies, and how to exercise your rights."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Freighthub is a static editorial site. It has no accounts, no forms, no newsletter and no
      analytics script. That removes most of the data a typical site collects — but not all of it, and
      this page states the rest plainly.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The operator of Freighthub is responsible for the processing described here. Contact:
      <a href="mailto:editor@freighthub.net">editor@freighthub.net</a>. The site does not publish a
      company registration or office address; that position is stated on the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> rather than filled with a placeholder.
    </p>

    <h2>What is processed</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>When</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Server logs: IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamp, response status</td>
          <td>Every request, generated by the hosting provider</td>
          <td>Deliver the page, keep the service available, detect abuse</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Email address and message content</td>
          <td>When you write to the editorial desk</td>
          <td>Answer your question, record a correction, keep a correspondence trail</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Anything you volunteer in that email</td>
          <td>At your choice</td>
          <td>Understand the question; not used for marketing</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      No account data, no payment data, no advertising identifiers and no cross-site tracking are
      collected, because none of those features exist on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Lawful basis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> in serving pages, keeping the site secure and answering correspondence.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> where you choose to send personal information in an email; you can withdraw it by asking us to delete the message.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics, advertising or session-recording
      script. The hosting provider may set a short-lived security cookie to distinguish browsers from
      bots; that cookie is essential to serving the site and is not used for profiling. Details are on
      the <a href="/cookies/">cookie page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Server logs are kept by the hosting provider for a short operational window, then discarded.</li>
      <li>Editorial correspondence is kept for up to 24 months so that a correction can be traced, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Corrections published on the site contain no personal data unless you ask to be named.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Data is shared only with the providers needed to run the site: the static hosting and CDN
      provider, and the email provider that receives editorial mail. It is not sold, rented or shared
      with advertisers or data brokers. A provider may process data outside your country; where that
      happens, the transfer relies on the provider's standard contractual terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or restrict the
      processing of your personal data, to object to processing based on legitimate interest, and to
      complain to a supervisory authority. Write to
      <a href="mailto:editor@freighthub.net">editor@freighthub.net</a>; requests are answered within 30
      days.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site is written for a professional audience and is not directed at children under 16.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Material changes to this policy are dated here. A change that affects what is collected will be
      noted on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a> as well.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
